---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Noticias from '../../components/Noticias.astro';
import Logos from '../../components/Logos.astro';
import Social from '../../components/Social.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Base titulo="Home" lang="en">
  <header class="post-header">
    <h1 class="post-title"><span class="negrita">APT</span>-GRAN</h1>
    <p class="post-description">Intelligent Attribution of Advanced Persistent Threats in Cybersecurity through Neural Networks and Graph Modelling.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="clearfix">
    <div class="profile">
      <div class="address">
        <p>University of Alcalá</p>
        <p>Own Research Programme</p>
        <p>2025 call · 12 months</p>
        <p>Ref. PIUAH25/IA-058</p>
        <p>PI: Enrique de la Hoz</p>
        <p>Co-PI: Laura M. Cornejo</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>
      APT-GRAN is a research project at the <a href="https://www.uah.es/en/">University of Alcalá</a> on the
      <strong>attribution</strong> of cyberattacks: determining which advanced persistent threat group is behind
      an intrusion from its observed activity.
    </p>
    <p>
      The starting point is a simple idea. An intrusion is naturally described as a network of related entities
      (tools, infrastructure, techniques, victims), and when several intrusions are analysed together some of
      those entities recur and connect them. Expert analysts spot these overlaps and weigh them by judgement. We
      investigate how to generalise that work with
      <a href={`${base}/en/proyecto`}>graph neural networks with attention mechanisms</a>, able to learn which
      relationships matter and how much.
    </p>
    <p>
      On this site we publish the project's <a href={`${base}/en/resultados`}>results</a> as they consolidate,
      its <a href={`${base}/en/publicaciones`}>publications</a> and the
      <a href={`${base}/en/recursos`}>datasets and software</a> we release so that experiments can be reproduced.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>news</h2>
  <Noticias lang="en" />
  <Logos lang="en" />
  <Social />
</Base>
